<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates softer as peso rates fall.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates softer as peso rates fall.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) dropped across the board on Wednesday following a fall on overnight call loan rates, traders said.</p>
<p>Peso interest rates eased after some four-billion peso worth of treasury notes matured. Liquidity also improved after heavy Central Bank buying of dollars on the foreign exchange market in recent days, traders said.</p>
<p>PHIBOR are average rates for foreign exchange forward quotes from 20 banks.</p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>		   Aug 28		  Aug 27</p>
<p>     1 W	 11  1/4		 11 1/2</p>
<p>     2 W	 11  1/4		 11 1/2</p>
<p>     1 M	 11  3/8		 11 1/2</p>
<p>     2 M	 11  7/16		11 9/16</p>
<p>     3 M	 11  7/16		11 9/16</p>
<p>     6 M	 11 11/16		11 3/4</p>
<p>     12M	 12			12 1/16</p>
<p>  DATE	     28-Aug		27-Aug</p>
<p>  VALUE	    29-Aug		28-Aug</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
